-----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. THIRD-PARTY CONTENT — NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENSE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Some material shipped alongside this site is the work of others and is
governed by its own terms:

  • Cited academic papers (Freud, Bowlby, Clasen, Blom, Jonason,
    Spiegel, Loewenstein, and the rest of the bibliography) remain
    the copyright of their respective authors and publishers. We
    cite them under the academic doctrine of fair use; we do not
    redistribute their full text.

  • Public-domain illustrations sourced from Wikimedia Commons,
    Vesalius's De humani corporis fabrica (1543), Boughton's 1893
    illustrations to "The Legend of Sleepy Hollow", and similar
    19th-century engravings are in the public domain. We do not
    claim copyright in those source images, only in any colour
    grading, composition, or framing work derived from them.

  • Web fonts (@fontsource/*) ship under the SIL Open Font License
    (OFL 1.1) or the open-source license specified by each package.
    See the respective node_modules/@fontsource/<font>/LICENSE files.

  • npm dependencies are governed by their own licenses; see
    pnpm-lock.yaml and each package's own LICENSE file.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------
4. NO AI TRAINING USE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

We do not consent to the use of any part of this work — code or
content — in the training, fine-tuning, or evaluation of machine
learning models without explicit prior written agreement. This
exclusion is asserted under:

  • robots.txt (Disallow for all major AI crawlers)
  • the X-Robots-Tag HTTP header
  • the EU Directive 2019/790, Article 4 (TDM opt-out)
  • the spirit of the CC BY-NC-SA license, under which commercial
    use — including the productisation of a model trained on this
    material — requires separate negotiation.


